(- Gmnotes: Roll in 10 Seconds: Use this when a player asks what to roll. ? Pick the) Tj
T*
(  trait that matches the approach. ? Set the Difficulty before the roll matters. ?) Tj
T*
(  State the stakes. ? Roll Hope d12 + Fear d12. ? Add trait, Experience, and bonuses.) Tj
T*
(  ? Compare total to Difficulty. Action Roll Results: Read total first, then Hope/Fear) Tj
T*
(  spin. ? Critical Success: best outcome, gain Hope, clear 1 Stress. ? Success with) Tj
T*
(  Hope: they get it and gain Hope. ? Success with Fear: they get it, but cost or) Tj
T*
(  pressure enters. ? Failure with Hope: they miss, but gain Hope and a useful thread.) Tj
T*
(  ? Failure with Fear: they miss and the GM makes a stronger move. Difficulty Ladder:) Tj
T*
(  Beginner hinges often sit around 10-14. ? Very Easy 5. ? Easy 10. ? Average 15. ?) Tj
T*
(  Hard 20. ? Very Hard 25. ? Nearly Impossible 30. Six Traits: Translate the fictional) Tj
T*
(  approach, not the D&D skill name. ? Agility: sprint, leap, maneuver. ? Strength:) Tj
T*
(  lift, smash, grapple. ? Finesse: control, hide, tinker. ? Instinct: perceive, sense,) Tj
T*
(  navigate. ? Presence: charm, perform, deceive. ? Knowledge: recall, analyze,) Tj
T*
(  comprehend. D&D to Daggerheart: Convert the instinct quickly, then move on. ?) Tj
T*
(  Perception -> Instinct. ? Saving throw/save -> Reaction...) Tj
